  "repair_or_experiment_note": "Human reported ordinary driving over small features makes the robot fly and lose stability. Retained started metadata and last coarse player snapshot: normal mode, about0.636m/s command,53.7degree tilt; no original command or contact trajectory exists. New remote4090 frozen diagnostic used task-isolated MuJoCo3.14 and ORT1.30 matching local versions; CPU physics and primary ONNX CPU inference on Linux4090 host, frozen TorchCUDA actor/gate references on the shared4090, not PhysX/GPU physics. V1 isolated pip install succeeded but import path failed before rollout; V2 explicit sys.path reused exact installed dependencies, six complete cases; V3 nine new command cases reproduced fixedE0 launch/fall at0.65 and1.0m/s. Actual0.5ms contact-force vectors sum to recorded root generalized constraint forces. Guide roller deeply contacts opposing40micrometre-thick quad/triangle prism surfaces; one step changes upward velocity by6.944m/s, not an MoE switching event. V4 nativeCCD-off completed four prefixes without the prior falls, then failed on an obsolete multiCCD enable enum; rc1/no wholeFINAL is preserved. V5 only missing four multiCCD-off cases used current disablebit524288 and completed FINAL; no old baseline/native-off replay. Both isolation branches remove the reproduced falls in their finite tests, at unchanged initial-stateSHA, geometry, gains, actuator limits, observations, frozen policies and commands. Candidate separate player entry disables multiCCD only and keeps nativeCCD, all original source/entry/terrain and experts intact; no original player or Isaac training hotpatch. Source-only local preparation and saved-array analysis, no local agent policy/physics test after4090 instruction. Preserve all local blank-line-anchor,6vertex-assumption, generated-label-newline errors and V2 corrections, original source, package install log, actual complete/prefix/error receipts, all producer artifactSHA, detailed forces and saved-result plot. Not exact original human replay, unique upstream bug proof, exact energy balance, all-terrain/jump/recovery qualification, or MoE training. Similar public upstream issue3691 is a hypothesis only. Record all outcomes, not only success.\n",
